  contentsAnswer: A few light clothes and a towel. Nothing else.
  weightAnswer: Four or five kilos, certainly no heavy equipment.
  metalAnswer: No tools or electronics; just the suitcase fittings.
  packingAnswer: Everything is tightly strapped. Nothing loose.
  responseAnswer: That movement must be the clothes settling. There is no mechanism.
  authorReasoning: 13 kg contradicts the confident light-load claim. Counterbalance/delayed
    pulse contradict both fixed packing and passive cloth. At least two independent
    clues.
